# @NAME@

@DESCRIPTION@

A DSP script, `product/script/@FILE@`, as a plugin of its own: the script
compiled as C++ and run by the same glue as the script player, on the
Supple Audio plugin framework @FRAMEWORK_VERSION@. It is the plugin the
player plays, with the same ID, parameters and state, so sessions and
presets made with one load in the other.

## Building

```sh
cmake --preset release
cmake --build --preset release
ctest --preset release
```

The built plugins are in `build/release/plugins/`. See
[framework/docs/BUILDING.md](framework/docs/BUILDING.md) for platforms,
sanitizers, validators and installing.

## Layout

- `product/script/@FILE@`: the script as it was written. It is ordinary
  C++ against `suite/runtime/include/supple/script.h`; change it there.
  The script compiler does not check it here, so what the player refuses
  (allocating in `process()`, an integer divided by a variable, ...) is
  yours to avoid.
- `product/Catalog.cpp`: makes the plugin from the script and lists each
  parameter's patch key, since C++ cannot see member names. List a `Param`
  you add there.
- `suite/`: the script runtime, the semantic-params layer and the glue;
  update it from a newer export with `suite/tools/update_suite.cmake`.
- `framework/`: the plugin framework, unchanged from the template; update
  it with `framework/tools/update_framework.cmake`.

